# Sets
@summary Stdlib Set — fromArray, union, intersection, difference, isSubset
@category stdlib

The Set module provides immutable unordered collections of unique values. Like dicts and arrays, every operation returns a new set rather than mutating the input.

Use fromArray to convert an Array into a Set (deduplicating in the process), and toArray to go back when you need ordered iteration.

## Building

fromArray(array) — convert an Array to a Set, removing duplicates.

setAdd(set, element) — return a new set with the element included. No-op if already present.

setRemove(set, element) — return a new set without the element. No-op if absent.

## Querying

size(set) — element count.

contains(set, element) — boolean check (the same name as the Array variant; dispatched on receiver type).

## Set algebra

union — produced by merging two sets. (No dedicated builtin — use fromArray(concat(toArray(a), toArray(b))) or build with setAdd.)

intersection(left, right) — elements in both.

difference(left, right) — elements in left but not in right.

isSubset(left, right) — true if every element of left is also in right.

## Conversion

toArray(set) — Array of elements. Order is implementation-defined; sort if you need a stable order.

--- example: dedupe.spn
-- Remove duplicates from an array via a round-trip through Set.
import Set (fromArray, toArray)
import Array (sort)

let raw = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6, 5, 3, 5]
let unique = sort(toArray(fromArray(raw)))
-- unique is [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 9]
unique
---

--- example: set-algebra.spn
-- Intersection and difference on tag sets.
import Set (fromArray, intersection, difference, isSubset)

let a = fromArray(["red", "green", "blue", "purple"])
let b = fromArray(["green", "yellow", "purple"])

let common = intersection(a, b)
let onlyInA = difference(a, b)
let aSubsetB = isSubset(a, b)

(common, onlyInA, aSubsetB)
-- (Set{"green","purple"}, Set{"red","blue"}, false)
---

--- example: incremental-build.spn
-- Build a set incrementally with setAdd; check membership with contains.
import Set (fromArray, setAdd, contains, size)

let visited = fromArray([])
visited = setAdd(visited, "/home")
visited = setAdd(visited, "/etc")
visited = setAdd(visited, "/home")  -- no-op: already present

let alreadySeen = contains(visited, "/home")
(size(visited), alreadySeen)
-- (2, true)
---

--- example: subset-check.spn
-- Verify that a required-feature set is satisfied by an available-feature set.
import Set (fromArray, isSubset)

let required = fromArray(["read", "write"])
let granted = fromArray(["read", "write", "admin"])

isSubset(required, granted)
-- true: every required permission is granted
---
